# What must not go into the image.
#
# The Dockerfile copies services/ and scripts/ and nothing else, so most of
# this is belt and braces -- but an image is a file anyone who can pull it can
# read, and the two things this repository has most of are screenshots of real
# job applications and live session cookies.

# Secrets and live sessions. None of these belong in an image; they arrive at
# runtime through --env-file and the volume.
.env
*.env
.chrome_profile/
.chrome_profile_test/
agent_profile/
**/cookies_vault.json
**/cookies_vault.prev.json
**/saved_cookies.json
**/cloud_account.json
**/portal_accounts.json
google_service_account.json
**/token.json
**/credentials.json

# Personal data. cv_master/ is deliberately absent from this list: it holds the
# master CV templates the tailor cuts from, and the entrypoint moves it onto
# the volume on first boot, where the generated per-account copies join it.
**/profile.json
**/profiles/
**/documents/
**/user_data/
**/candidate_vault.json
**/*.pdf
**/*.docx

# State that belongs on the volume, not in the layer.
**/*.db
**/applications.jsonl
**/geocode_cache.json
**/browser_use_cache.json

# Weight with no purpose.
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.github/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.backup/
scratch/
test_data/
tests/
ios/
expo-mapjob/
MapJOB_browser-extension/
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.html
*.log
**/screenshots/

